Package: gistsurv
Title: Site- and Age-Stratified Survival and Competing-Risk Analysis for
    GIST
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Yue", "Yang", , "yueyangve8@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reusable functions for the site- and age-stratified survival
    analysis of gastrointestinal stromal tumour (GIST) cohorts assembled
    from the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) programme.
    The package wraps the steps used in the underlying cohort study:
    preparation of survival and competing-risk outcome variables, baseline
    characteristic tables, Kaplan-Meier estimation, Cox proportional
    hazards models together with proportional-hazards diagnostics,
    restricted mean survival time (RMST), side-by-side comparison of the
    three effect estimators (hazard ratio, Kaplan-Meier probability and
    RMST difference), and competing-risk analysis through cumulative
    incidence functions and Fine-Gray models. Any example data shipped
    with the package are simulated and contain no real patient records; no
    SEER data are included or redistributed.
